<title>BELGIUM: De Silguy says UK budget will decide EMU criterion.</title>
<headline>De Silguy says UK budget will decide EMU criterion.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said on Wednesday that Britain's next budget could trim the country's deficit to GDP ratio to 3 percent in 1997, thus meeting the Maastricht criteria for a single currency.</p>
<p>He told a news conference a Commission forecast of 3.5 percent for Britain was calculated without knowledge of Britain's next budget plans.</p>
<p>De Silguy noted that Britain based its annual budgets on the financial year rather than the calendar year and that such differences could accound for 0.5 to 0.7 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>BRUSSELS NEWSROOM: +32 2 287-6830</p>
